cff-version: 1.2.0
type: software
title: 20-bit two-stage SAR ADC digital IP and Python transaction model
message: >-
  Cite this software and the Git commit used for a result. Cite the ISSCC paper
  separately when referring to the published converter architecture.
authors:
  - family-names: Zhao
    given-names: Reed
    alias: defineiocc02
    affiliation: Xidian University
version: "9.0.1+adi.repro"
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/defineiocc02/20bit_SAR_ADC_Behaviour_Verification"
url: "https://github.com/defineiocc02/20bit_SAR_ADC_Behaviour_Verification"
abstract: >-
  SystemVerilog digital controller and Python transaction model for an
  independent reproduction of a two-stage precision SAR converter. The model
  records physical slice selection, dither switches, resolved SAR decisions,
  ADC2 codes and weighted digital reconstruction. The software documentation
  identifies the engineering assumptions used for the analogue macro responses.
keywords:
  - sar-adc
  - digital-ip
  - behavioural-model
  - dynamic-element-matching
  - dither
